##Application Load Balancer - This is a networking component that intelligently routes HTTP traffic across mutiple backend targets
##Auto scaling group - An AWS services that automatically manages the number of EC2 instances running in an application

##How ASG and ALB Work Together
While an Application Load Balancer (ALB) handles traffic distribution, an Auto Scaling Group handles compute capacity. In a production architecture, they are tightly integrated:

Traffic Inflow: Client requests hit the ALB.

Target Group Routing: The ALB forwards requests to the instances managed by the ASG.

Automatic Registration: When the ASG launches a new EC2 instance due to a traffic spike, that instance automatically registers itself with the ALB's Target Group. Once it passes health checks, it begins receiving live traffic.

Deregistration: When traffic drops and the ASG terminates an instance, it gracefully deregisters the instance from the ALB so no active requests are dropped.
